  "description_html": "Size comparison of members of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parankylosauria\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Parankylosauria\">Parankylosauria</a> (<i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antarctopelta\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Antarctopelta\">Antarctopelta</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kunbarrasaurus\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Kunbarrasaurus\">Kunbarrasaurus</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stegouros\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Stegouros\">Stegouros</a></i>, and <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patagopelta\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Patagopelta\">Patagopelta</a></i>) with an adult human male (~1.8 m) for reference. \n<p><b>Note:</b> Recent and ongoing research suggests that <i>Patagopelta</i> belongs in this group (hence its inclusion), although initial assessments suggested nodosaurid affinities.\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"References\">References</h3></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"_Antarctopelta_(holotype)\"><span id=\"_Antarctopelta_.28holotype.29\"></span><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#800C0E\" title=\"#800C0E\"> </b> <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antarctopelta\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Antarctopelta\">Antarctopelta</a></i> <small style=\"font-size:85%;\">(holotype)</small></h4></div>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.12429%2Fj.advps.2023.0036\">\"A new look at the first dinosaur discovered in Antarctica: reappraisal of <i>Antarctopelta oliveroi</i> (Ankylosauria: Parankylosauria)\"</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/255615919_Reappraisal_of_an_ankylosaurian_dinosaur_from_the_Upper_Cretaceous_of_James_Ross_Island_Antarctica\">\"Reappraisal of an ankylosaurian dinosaur from the Upper Cretaceous of James Ross Island (Antarctica)\"</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-021-04147-1\">\"Bizarre tail weaponry in a transitional ankylosaur from subantarctic Chile\"</a></li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"_Kunbarrasaurus_(holotype)\"><span id=\"_Kunbarrasaurus_.28holotype.29\"></span><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#B15E4C\" title=\"#B15E4C\"> </b> <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kunbarrasaurus\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Kunbarrasaurus\">Kunbarrasaurus</a></i> <small style=\"font-size:85%;\">(holotype)</small></h4></div>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://dx.doi.org/10.7717%2Fpeerj.1475\">Cranial osteology of the ankylosaurian dinosaur formerly known as <i>Minmi</i> sp. (Ornithischia: Thyreophora) from the Lower Cretaceous Allaru Mudstone of Richmond, Queensland, Australia</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/plastospleen/art/Kunbarrasaurus-ieversi-Skeletal-848278360\"><i>Kunbarrasaurus</i> skeletal diagram</a> by Ashley Patch</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/partpdf/303873\">\"Preliminary report on a new ankylosaur from the Early Cretaceous of Queensland, Australia\"</a></li>\n<li>\"Armor of the small ankylosaur <i>Minmi</i>\" in <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://archive.org/details/armoreddinosaurs0000unse_u1v7\">\"<i>The Armored Dinosaurs</i>\"</a></li>\n<li>\"Bizarre tail weaponry...\"</li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"_Stegouros_(holotype)\"><span id=\"_Stegouros_.28holotype.29\"></span><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#DBB091\" title=\"#DBB091\"> </b> <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stegouros\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Stegouros\">Stegouros</a></i> <small style=\"font-size:85%;\">(holotype)</small></h4></div>\n<ul><li>\"Bizarre tail weaponry...\"</li>\n<li><cite class=\"book\" style=\"font-style:normal\" id=\"Reference-Paul-2024\">Paul, Gregory S. (2024)      <i> The Princeton Field Guide to Dinosaurs</i> (3rd ed.), Princeton, N.J.:  Princeton University Press  <small><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:ISBN\"><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">ISBN</span></a></span>:  <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0-691-23157-0\" title=\"Special:BookSources/978-0-691-23157-0\">978-0-691-23157-0</a>. </small></cite></li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"_Patagopelta_(various_specimens)\"><span id=\"_Patagopelta_.28various_specimens.29\"></span><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#E53636\" title=\"#E53636\"> </b> <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patagopelta\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Patagopelta\">Patagopelta</a></i> <small style=\"font-size:85%;\">(various specimens)</small></h4></div>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1080/14772019.2022.2137441\">\"A new small-bodied ankylosaurian dinosaur from the Upper Cretaceous of North Patagonia (Río Negro Province, Argentina)\"</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jsames.2019.102320\">\"New ankylosaur (Thyreophora, ornithischia) remains from the Upper Cretaceous of Patagonia\"</a></li>\n<li>\"South American ankylosaurs\" in <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://archive.org/details/armoreddinosaurs0000unse_u1v7\">\"<i>The Armored Dinosaurs</i>\"</a></li>\n<li>\"Bizarre tail weaponry...\"</li>\n<li><i>Kunbarrasaurus</i>...by Ashley Patch</li>\n<li>\"Cranial osteology...\"</li></ul>",
